{number: 70}
{title: Take My Life, and Let It Be}
{key: F}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[F] Take my life, and let it be
Consecrated, [C7] Lord, to [F] Thee;
Take my moments and my [Bb] days;
Let them [F] flow in [C7] ceaseless [F] praise.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[F] Take my hands, and let them move
At the impulse [C7] of Thy [F] love;
Take my feet, and let them [Bb] be
Swift and [F] beautiful [C7] for [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[F] Take my voice, and let me sing
Always, only, [C7] for my [F] King;
Take my lips, and let them [Bb] be
Filled with [F] messages [C7] from [F] Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
[F] Take my will, and make it Thine;
It shall be no [C7] longer [F] mine;
Take my heart, it is Thine [Bb] own;
It shall [F] be Thy [C7] royal [F] throne.
{end_of_verse}
